(a) Subject to the limitations of subsection (b) of this section, the redevelopment authority may exercise any powers necessary or convenient to carry out the purposes of the Redevelopment Powers Law (Ga. Laws 1985, p. 1360, § 1), including, but not limited to, the power to:
(1) Describe the boundaries of one or more redevelopment areas within its area of operation, but any redevelopment area so described shall conform to the definition of a redevelopment area provided by O.C.G.A. § 36-44-3(7) (Ga. Laws 1989, p. 1398, § 1);
(2) Cause redevelopment plans to be prepared, to approve by resolution the plans, and to implement the provisions and effectuate the purposes of the plans;
(3) Create within redevelopment areas tax allocation districts and define the boundaries thereof or designate an entire redevelopment area as a tax allocation district;
(4) Define the boundaries of portions of a redevelopment area or an entire redevelopment area for the implementation of redevelopment plans other than plans calling for the creation of tax allocation districts;
(5) Issue tax allocation bonds;
(6) Deposit moneys into and disburse moneys from the special fund of any tax allocation district;
(7) Enter into and execute any contracts, leases, mortgages or other agreements, including agreements with bondholders or lenders, determined by the board of commissioners to be necessary or convenient to implement the provisions and effectuate the purposes of redevelopment plans. The contracts or agreements may include conditions, restrictions or covenants that either run with the land or otherwise regulate the use of land;
(8) Acquire and retain or acquire and dispose of property of the authority or interests therein for redevelopment purposes or use, or dispose of property or interests therein presently owned by the authority; and any disposition of such property or interests therein may be by public or private sale or lease; and
(9) Exercise, for the purposes of this article, any powers conferred upon the county by O.C.G.A. § 36-61-1 et seq., the Urban Redevelopment Law.
(b) The powers granted to the authority by subsection (a) of this section may be exercised only for the purpose of adopting or implementing redevelopment plans, but this limitation shall not be construed to interfere with the exercise of any power now or hereafter delegated to the authority by the county that is granted to the county by any other law.
(c) The redevelopment powers delegated to the authority shall be limited by the following requirements:
(1) Any redevelopment plan must be approved by resolution of the board of commissioners as a condition precedent to the implementation of said redevelopment plan, and such approval shall be subject to the requirements of O.C.G.A. § 36-44-7.
(2) The boundaries of any redevelopment area must be described by resolution of the board of commissioners.
(3) A tax allocation district must be created by resolution of the board of commissioners.
(4) The issuance of any tax allocation bonds shall be by resolution of the board of commissioners.
(5) The power of eminent domain may only be exercised under this article by the board of commissioners.
(6) The authority shall not exercise any redevelopment project powers except those which may be conferred on an urban redevelopment agency under O.C.G.A. § 36-61-17 of the Urban Redevelopment Law (O.C.G.A. § 36-44-6, enacted by Ga. Laws 1985, p. 1360, § 1).
(Code 1973, § 2-20-79)

